+/*
+ * Small paths drawn smooth (VitaSurf).
+ *
+ * libnsfb strokes a path as one-pixel steps and fills it with whole
+ * pixels, and its stroke width is a whole number: an icon drawn with a
+ * 1.33 pixel line -- a 24-unit Lucide icon at 16 pixels -- came out as
+ * a thin, jagged line one pixel wide, dim beside the same icon in any
+ * other browser. Its path also ran a line from the end of each subpath
+ * to the start of the next.
+ *
+ * A path whose box is small enough is drawn here instead: how much of
+ * each pixel the stroke or the fill covers is worked out, and the path
+ * is plotted as a bitmap of its colour with that much alpha. A stroke
+ * covers what lies within half its width of the line, which gives the
+ * round joins and caps the icon sets draw with; a fill is sampled at
+ * four heights a pixel, each span measured exactly across, by the
+ * nonzero rule SVG fills with. A larger path is left to libnsfb.
+ */
+#define FB_AA_MAX_AREA (256 * 256)
+#define FB_AA_MAX_POINTS 4096
